  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Logan Webb lasted 2.2 innings, Boston scored five in the third, and the Giants clawed back with three of their own but never found the lead they needed.",
    "what_this_means": "This team doesn't have the cushion to surrender a game early and hope to catch it late. Webb exited before he should have, leaving the bullpen to hold a deficit. Something Sanmartin and Foley managed across 4.0 scoreless innings, but the offense couldn't convert the charity. They left two runners on in the second, when the game was still tied, and never got another real chance. Drew Gilbert's home run mattered; it cut the gap to one and proved the bats existed. But two runs on 7 hits isn't a plan. The Fenway wind didn't beat them. Poor execution in the third and empty at-bats in spots that mattered did.",
    "what_to_watch": "Patrick Sandoval takes the ball tonight against Blade Tidwell. Sandoval's ERA sits at 4.76. Boston's rotation hasn't been crisp. The Giants need to put early pressure on and not let another game slip away on a short outing.",
